3F  03   6	INQUIRY DATA HAS CHANGED
print_FRU

3F  80   6	****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR  ****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR ****
		One or more drives in the disk array has been marked DOWN
		due to detection of the following error:
		DRIVE DOWNED BECAUSE OF A FAILED WRITE OPERATION
		The drive(s) should be replaced as soon as possible to
		avoid the possibility of data loss or corruption.
		- This is the result of an error that prevents access to
		  user data on this drive.  This may result in erroneous
		  data being read/written.  (ex. An Unrecovered Write
		  Error)
		***********************************************************
print_FRU

3F  81   6	****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR  ****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR ****
		One or more drives in the disk array has been marked DOWN
		due to detection of the following error:
		AUTOMATIC REALLOCATION OF RECOVERED DRIVE ERROR FAILED
		The drive(s) should be replaced as soon as possible to
		avoid the possibility of data loss or corruption.
		- Either reassign block or recovery of data on the re-
		  assigned sector failed.
		***********************************************************
print_FRU

3F  82   6	****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR  ****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR ****
		RECONSTRUCTION FAILED - ERROR ON DRIVE BEING RECONSTRUCTED
		This condition requires that the drive be replaced as soon
		as possible.  User data is still available by using parity,
		but a second failure at this time will result in loss of
		user data for the entire LUN (RAID 5), or will result in an
		unrecoverable error (other RAID levels).
		- The reconstruction operation cannot complete because of
		  an unrecoverable write error or a failed drive format
		  (before reconstruction starts) on the drive being recon-
		  structed.  It must be replaced (again) before the recon-
		  struction can be retried.
		***********************************************************
print_FRU

3F  83   6	****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR  ****  CRITICAL ARRAY ERROR  ****
		RECONSTRUCTION FAILED - ERROR ON DRIVE REQUIRED FOR RECON-
		STRUCTION.
		The reconstruction operation cannot complete because of an
		unrecoverable read error on one of the drives needed for
		reconstruction.  The array can still be run in degraded
		mode, but if user data is stored at the address in error
		it cannot be read.  A back-up of the array should be attemp-
		ted to recover the remaining data.  To bring the LUN to an
		optimal state, the failed drive must be replaced, the array
		must be formatted, and the data must be restored from a
		back-up (the one just made or a previous successful back-up).
		*************************************************************
print_FRU

3F  84   6	***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***
		DRIVE FAILED DUE TO A HARDWARE COMPONENT DIAGNOSTICS FAILURE
		This condition requires that the drive be replaced as soon as
		possible.  User data is still available by using parity, but
		a second failure at this time (when a drive has been downed)
		will result in the loss of data for the entire Lun (Raid 5)
		or will result in an unrecoverable error (other raid levels).
print_FRU

3F  85   6	***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***  WARNING  ***
		DRIVE FAILED BECAUSE IT FAILED A TEST UNIT READY COMMAND
		(DURING START OF DAY) OR IT FAILED A READ CAPACITY COMMAND
		(DURING START OF DAY OR DURING A FORMAT OR RECONSTRUCTION
		OPERATION)
		This condition requires that the drive be replaced as soon as
		possible.  User data is still available by using parity, but
		a second failure at this time (when a drive has been downed)
		will result in the loss of data for the entire Lun (Raid 5)
		or will result in an unrecoverable error (other raid levels).
print_FRU

